{"file_name": "screenshot_5_creature.png", "id": "1559818478978287", "uri": "https://scontent-sea5-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/613094043_1559818482311620_1858277794794842808_n.png?_nc_cat=110&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=LmSwuEuYnB8Q7kNvwGkqtO2&_nc_oc=AdpyQ9Tha_5WQkQb7Ia2Mx4ESXVc4-n3TpdrFKTamOIO44dJCCf17p3YiHWwIBl-xiI&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-sea5-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_AQTbC1xbx1rQGQvCv-_3-nxoSBIqVhLA-48uAqrsYYOUbA&oe=6B09B7CA"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "Clayground", "keywords": ["art", "sculpt", "3d", "clay"], "long_description": "Clayground is true volumetric clay sculpting on Meta Quest.\nPaint infinite clay with zero polygon anxiety, on an unbounded canvas that grows wherever you sculpt. Capture any part of your sculpt as a stamp. Sculpt in mixed-reality passthrough at your real desk. Export to Blender with one press.", "short_description": "Real clay. Your room. Sculpt without limits."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://emotionull.art/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/privacy-policy.html", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "Emotionull", "support_website_url": null, "website_url": "https://emotionull.art/", "category": null, "comfort_rating": "COMFORTABLE_FOR_MOST", "comfort_tags": [], "context_category": {"id": "362692211442873", "context_category": "APPS"}, "context_topics": [{"id": "1819021644882647"}], "external_subscription_type": "NOT_REQUIRED", "genres": [], "has_in_app_ads": null, "internet_connection": "NOT_REQUIRED", "play_area": "NO_MOVEMENT", "recommended_graphics": null, "recommended_memory_gb": null, "recommended_processor": null, "supported_in_app_languages": ["en"], "supported_input_devices": ["OCULUS_TOUCH"], "supported_player_modes": ["SITTING", "STANDING", "ROOM_SCALE"], "supported_tracking_modes": [], "user_interaction_modes": ["SINGLE_USER"], "id": "1345650630966511"}}]}, "scheduled_offers": {"count": 1, "nodes": [{"status": "PUBLISHED", "id": "888881050951536"}]}, "baseline_offer": {"id": "888881050951536"}, "is_approved": true, "firstOffer": {"nodes": [{"start_time": 1785211200, "status": "PUBLISHED", "id": "888881050951536"}]}, "liveChannel": {"nodes": [{"latest_supported_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "id": "1459767322888174", "version": "0.2.364"}, "id": "1278478724173176", "channel_name": "LIVE"}]}, "is_for_oculus_keys_only": false, "primary_binaries": {"nodes": [{"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "1345650624299845", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "1459767322888174"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1278478724173176"}]}, "change_log": "New\r\n\r\nConnect to clayvr.com: Capture > clayvr.com > Connect links your headset to your Clayground account with your Meta account. No code to type. If Meta can't confirm you yet, the headset shows a short code to enter at clayvr.com/workspace.\r\nOnce connected, Send latest GLB puts your newest export in your account in one press, privately, and your account's reference images show up in References.\r\n24 new stamps: a Mannequin, Torso, Arm and Leg to block out a figure; a four-legged body, Wing, Tail, Horn, Claw, Tentacle, Fin and Scales; Cone, Wedge, Tube, Bowl, Hex bar, Arch, Stairs and Spring; a Gear, Bolt, Chain link and Bone.\r\nA new look: rounded dark menus and solid highlights. Everything is where it was. Prefer the old one? Preferences > Look: Classic.\r\nCel shading: Preferences > Cel shading draws your sculpt like a cartoon.\r\nPhotos with a transparent background: Preferences > Photo: Cutout.\r\nChoose where the tool tip sits: Comfort > Tip (Handle, Between, Pointer or Pencil).\r\n\r\nBetter\r\n\r\nStamps work like Clay: press B twice to switch a stamp between Add and Erase. Big stamps now use far less of a layer's room.\r\nThe tool wheel shows a green plus or red minus for Add and Erase, and which way Swirl turns.\r\nThe brush has a dark edge, so you can see it on a light backdrop.\r\nStarter stamps have proper pictures, so a nose looks like a nose.\r\nMirror stays how you left it when you start a new sculpt.\r\nChanging tools by accident? Comfort > Wheel: Click only changes tool when you pull the trigger.\r\n\r\nFixed\r\n\r\nThe view could keep spinning after you let go of your sculpt. Spin is now off unless you turn it on at Comfort > Spin.\r\nThe welcome card and your clay could appear behind you when the app opened.\r\nPhotos no longer show up twice in your Quest gallery.", "created_date": 1795381188, "id": "1459767322888174", "version": "0.2.364", "version_code": 364, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "1345650624299845", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "1459767322888174"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1278478724173176"}]}, "change_log": "Found it. A feature called Spin was keeping the view turning if you let go while your hand was still moving. In today's update (0.2.360) it's off unless you turn it on. If you're still on the old build, switch it off now at Preferences > Comfort > Spin. Tell me if it still happens after the update.", "created_date": 1795289583, "id": "1458696012995305", "version": "0.2.360", "version_code": 360, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "1345650624299845", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "1459767322888174"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1278478724173176"}]}, "change_log": "Comfort > Tip now cycles Handle, Between, Pointer, Pencil. Pencil is the Pointer direction swung 40\u00b0 to the inside of the hand, so the tip sits about 6 cm to the left for a right hand and mirrors for Lefty.", "created_date": 1795213414, "id": "1457791856419054", "version": "0.2.359", "version_code": 359, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "1345650624299845", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "1459767322888174"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1278478724173176"}]}, "change_log": "A new look: rounded dark menus, solid highlights on what is selected, and every tool listed first on the Tools page. Everything is where it was. Prefer the old one? Preferences > Look: Classic, then reopen Clayground.\r\nFixed: when you opened Clayground, the welcome card and your clay could appear behind you or facing the wrong way. They now come to where you are looking.\r\nCel shading: Preferences > Cel shading draws your sculpt like a cartoon, in flat bands of light with a dark edge.\r\nChoose where the tool tip sits: Comfort > Tip. Handle (as before), Between, or Pointer, for holding the controller like a pen or a microphone.\r\nPhotos with a transparent background: Preferences > Photo: Cutout saves your sculpt as a PNG with nothing behind it. And photos no longer show up twice in your Quest gallery.\r\nChanging tools by accident? Try Comfort > Wheel: Click. The tool wheel then only changes tool when you point at one and pull the trigger. Also fixed a cut-off message on an empty Files page.", "created_date": 1795149138, "id": "1457001849831388", "version": "0.2.358", "version_code": 358, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "1345650624299845", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "1459767322888174"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1278478724173176"}]}, "change_log": "hand tracking fixes", "created_date": 1794763063, "id": "1452776083587298", "version": "0.2.354", "version_code": 354, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}]}}, "viewer": {"user": null}}}